From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:40:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] compositor: compose scaled layers on the CPU band path
 (T-505)

The CPU band path (JihadCpuDraw) composed only layers whose transform is a
whole-pixel translation, so a zoomed page fell back to the GPU for the
whole frame. With JIHAD_GPU_CPU_SCALE=1 it now also takes a layer under a
uniform scale: JihadCpuDrawScaled samples the band's rows in layer pixels
(one extra row each side), a two-pass filter (NEON vertical, packed
horizontal on ARM) writes each row once into write-through memory, and the
weights round with vrshrn so a full-weight sum of 256 stays in range (the
seventh build divided by 255 and overflowed bands to black). Off by
default until the device rounds give their verdict; the band statistics
line now counts scaled layers separately.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MpagfP34fXBdsc76E8YSzR
---
 gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp | 276 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 260 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

